#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_arima_burst_search.ipynb:10002
#: 7f916bee5cce4a20ba24c0e5b6325030
msgid "ARIMA-Based Burst Detection"
msgstr "ARIMA を用いたバーストイベント検出"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_arima_burst_search.ipynb:10003
#: 2089273afb0c43b79567c93a4f8dd853
msgid "Idea sketch for burst gravitational-wave searches"
msgstr "バースト重力波探索のアイデアスケッチ"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_arima_burst_search.ipynb:10005
#: 4b2827034b314805a0331a89d256d842
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "はじめに"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_arima_burst_search.ipynb:10006
#: 0baabc00e46b426faf34267121a4db88
msgid ""
"Detector data are dominated by approximately stationary background noise, "
"while burst gravitational waves (for example from core-collapse supernovae) "
"appear as short, non-stationary transients embedded in that noise."
msgstr ""
"検出器データは近似的に定常な背景ノイズに支配されており、バースト重力波（例：コアコラプス超新星由来）はそのノイズ中に埋め込まれた短時間の非定常過渡現象として現れます。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_arima_burst_search.ipynb:10008
#: 02800070a4b44b079b0a55a65a165298
msgid ""
"This notebook demonstrates the idea of using an **autoregressive model "
"(ARIMA)** to learn the stationary background and make burst-like residuals "
"stand out. It is a simple example of an unmodeled search strategy that does "
"not rely on waveform templates."
msgstr ""
"本ノートブックでは、**自己回帰モデル（ARIMA）** "
"を用いて定常背景を学習し、バースト的な残差を際立たせるアイデアを示します。これは波形テンプレートに依存しない、アンモデルド探索戦略の基本的な例です。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_arima_burst_search.ipynb:10010
#: 6cdd43fdf068422aa68feec8916bf9f4
msgid "References"
msgstr "参考文献"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_arima_burst_search.ipynb:10011
#: 0c1acff7725642ea988d246343ba9360
msgid ""
"Autoregressive Search of Gravitational Waves: Denoising (ARIMA_DeNoise.pdf)"
msgstr ""
"Autoregressive Search of Gravitational Waves: Denoising (ARIMA_DeNoise.pdf)"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_arima_burst_search.ipynb:10012
#: 2ba3493828f64d2fb88733dde452a79d
msgid "BEACON: Autoregressive Search for Unmodeled transients (BEACON.pdf)"
msgstr "BEACON: Autoregressive Search for Unmodeled transients (BEACON.pdf)"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_arima_burst_search.ipynb:10013
#: 8a9ce90441174e64a50d0f463696eb24
msgid "Sparkler: Autoregressive Search of Unmodeled GW (Sparkler_1min.pdf)"
msgstr "Sparkler: Autoregressive Search of Unmodeled GW (Sparkler_1min.pdf)"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_arima_burst_search.ipynb:30002
#: 597b9ac173544aefb853ec493110e407
msgid "1. Generate detector noise"
msgstr "1\\. 検出器ノイズの生成"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_arima_burst_search.ipynb:30003
#: f1a270a3f96742dcb6b3db8f466cc42a
msgid ""
"First we simulate detector background noise. When available we use an aLIGO "
"design-sensitivity model; otherwise we fall back to generic colored noise."
msgstr ""
"まず検出器の背景ノイズをシミュレートします。aLIGO "
"設計感度モデルが利用可能な場合はそれを使用し、利用できない場合は汎用カラードノイズにフォールバックします。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_arima_burst_search.ipynb:50002
#: 8100e9bbb5c44813b0b87a36947c2ff5
msgid "2. Inject a burst signal"
msgstr "2\\. バースト信号の注入"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_arima_burst_search.ipynb:50003
#: decbe106f36a4d419bae300f999c6fd2
msgid ""
"We inject a sine-Gaussian burst into the second half of the data and use it "
"as the test segment."
msgstr "サイン・ガウスバーストをデータの後半に注入し、それをテストセグメントとして使用します。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_arima_burst_search.ipynb:70002
#: fea484bd791d4e1486782d5bba20bb68
msgid "3. Learn the background with ARIMA"
msgstr "3\\. ARIMA による背景学習"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_arima_burst_search.ipynb:70003
#: 0c222ebae49346d990ab46ee25ffbd5a
msgid ""
"We fit an ARIMA model on the first 8 seconds, where no burst is present, so "
"that the model captures the stationary background statistics. The data are "
"moderately downsampled to keep the example lightweight."
msgstr ""
"バーストが存在しない最初の 8 秒間のデータに ARIMA "
"モデルをフィットし、定常背景の統計的特性をモデルが学習できるようにします。例を軽量に保つため、データは適度にダウンサンプリングされます。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_arima_burst_search.ipynb:90002
#: 72c01f91928b4e35845caa58896fa874
msgid "4. Compute residuals and detect anomalies"
msgstr "4\\. 残差の計算と異常検出"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_arima_burst_search.ipynb:90003
#: e1adaea79a2e420898dfbea698d18e43
msgid ""
"We apply the fitted model to the remaining data and inspect the residuals. "
"Stationary noise should leave small residuals, while an unmodeled burst "
"produces a localized excess."
msgstr ""
"フィットしたモデルを残りのデータに適用し、残差を調べます。定常ノイズでは残差が小さく収まりますが、モデル化されていないバーストが存在すると局所的な過剰が生じます。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_arima_burst_search.ipynb:110002
#: 6128398ffc0945089b053e640bb1672a
msgid "5. Evaluate performance versus SNR"
msgstr "5\\. SNR に対する性能評価"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_arima_burst_search.ipynb:110003
#: 7083ff1ac9ae4570afc9e333c7f8a2de
msgid ""
"Finally we repeat the injection for several signal-to-noise ratios to "
"estimate how the residual-based detection responds as the burst becomes "
"weaker."
msgstr "最後に、さまざまな信号対雑音比でバースト注入を繰り返し、バーストが弱くなるにつれて残差ベースの検出がどのように応答するかを推定します。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_arima_burst_search.ipynb:130002
#: b37699f565024e3e9b6ab3017c220f31
msgid "Summary"
msgstr "まとめ"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_arima_burst_search.ipynb:130004
#: ccd9ef69f97b4d5d82ad1c045c3d5d6a
msgid "Key ideas behind ARIMA-based burst searches"
msgstr "ARIMA を用いたバースト探索の核心的なアイデア"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_arima_burst_search.ipynb:130005
#: 81b38eeb42d9410488552fad51069939
msgid ""
"**Background suppression**: model and subtract stationary noise to improve "
"the visibility of weak transients."
msgstr "**背景抑制**: 定常ノイズをモデル化・差し引きすることで、弱い過渡現象の視認性を向上させる。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_arima_burst_search.ipynb:130006
#: bbc859207cfe466a81ebf0a12a557c3e
msgid ""
"**Residual analysis**: monitor deviations from the expected residual "
"distribution to identify unmodeled events."
msgstr "**残差解析**: 期待される残差分布からの逸脱を監視し、モデル化されていないイベントを同定する。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_arima_burst_search.ipynb:130008
#: 9288a6e93fa24c4ea3a81b30dfd6353b
msgid ""
"Production pipelines such as BEACON extend this idea to multiple channels "
"and coherence checks, but this notebook captures the core intuition in a "
"compact example."
msgstr ""
"BEACON "
"などの本番パイプラインはこのアイデアを複数チャンネルおよびコヒーレンスチェックへと拡張していますが、本ノートブックはその核心的な直観をコンパクトな例で示しています。"
